The 2nd December, 2025 
           This is an application for discharging the rule on the ground that 
the respondent No. 2, in the meantime, disposed of the petitioner’s 
representation dated 29.07.2018 as directed by this court.  
Mr. Md. Raju Mia, learned Advocate for the respondent No. 3-
applicant-bank by filing an application submits that the instant writ petition 
was filed challenging an auction under section 12(3) of the Artha Rin Adalat 
Ain, 2003 and at the time of issuance of the rule, the court passed an interim 
order of stay of the auction for sale of the mortgaged property for a limited 
period which expired on 05.09.2018 and the petitioner did not take any steps 
to extend the order of stay. He next submits that at the time of issuance of 
rule this court directed the respondent No. 2 namely Governor, Bangladesh 
Bank to dispose of the petitioner’s representation dated 29.07.2018 as 
evident in (Annexure-C) to the writ petition and the said respondent No. 2 
already disposed of the same within that period. Therefore, the learned 

<<PAGE 2>>
2 
 
Advocate for the respondent No. 3 applicant- bank prays for discharging the 
rule as being infructuous for ends of justice. 
The application is not opposed. 
We have heard the learned Advocate for the respondent No. 3-
applicant bank. We have gone through the application and the relevant order 
dated 05.08.2018. 
Since the respondent No. 2, namely Governor, Bangladesh Bank has 
already disposed of the petitioner’s representation dated 29.07.2018 as 
evident in Annexure-I to the application for discharging the rule and the 
interim order of stay of the auction for sale of the mortgaged property 
expired on 05.09.2018 therefore, the instant rule has become infructuous.  
In view of the facts and circumstances, we are inclined to allow the 
instant application and accordingly, the same is allowed. 
Accordingly, the rule is discharged as being infructuous. 
 
                                                         (Sikder Mahmudur Razi, J.) 
 
 
                                                                   (Raziuddin Ahmed, J.) 
","The PETITIONER brought a writ against the STATE and other RESPONDENTS concerning an auction for sale of mortgaged property under section 12(3) of the Artha Rin Adalat Ain, 2003. When issuing the Rule, the court directed RESPONDENT No. 2, the central-bank authority, to determine the PETITIONER’S representation dated 29.07.2018 and imposed a temporary stay of the auction. RESPONDENT No. 3, the creditor bank, now applies for termination of the Rule. It contends that the representation has been determined as directed and that the stay expired on 05.09.2018 without any step to extend it. The application asserts that these developments leave no continuing subject for adjudication and seeks closure of the proceedings in the interests of justice.",Not stated,REFUSED,"The court examined the application and the order dated 05.08.2018 concerning the PETITIONER’S representation. It found that the competent RESPONDENT had already determined that representation in compliance with the direction accompanying the Rule. It also found that the temporary protection against the auction of the mortgaged property had expired on 05.09.2018 and had not been extended. On those facts, the court considered the controversy infructuous: the requested administrative determination had occurred and the interim protection was no longer operative. Its reasoning rested on these intervening circumstances rather than on an interpretation of the auction statute.",4f93684db62fcf4686d5ec7a4cc78dca5fee9da02df8b3024ffcc70d1ede937b
