The 2nd December, 2025 
           This is an application for discharging the rule.  
Mr. Mohammad Mosfequs Salehin, learned Advocate for the respondent 
Nos. 2 and 3-applicants by filing an application submits that the petitioner has 
challenged the non-compliance with the order of the Ministry of Commerce 
regarding the refund of the Performance Security amounting to Tk. 
1,47,49,200/- deposited with Social Islami bank Limited, Shyamoli Branch, 
Dhaka. He next submits that subsequently the petitioner in the instant writ 
petition has filed another writ petition being Writ Petition No. 10597 of 2024, 
challenging the letter of encashment dated 19.08.2024 and both the matters are 
connected with the same Performance Guarantee of Tk. 1,47,49,200/- and 
relates to Contract No. 24/21-22 hence, the rule issued in the instant writ petition 
has become infructuous. 
The application is not opposed.  
We have heard the learned Advocate for the respondent Nos. 2 and 3-
applicants. We have gone through the application, grounds taken thereon as well 
as the writ petition. 

<<PAGE 2>>
2 
 
It appears that the grievance raised in the present writ petition is 
concerning possible encashment of the Bank Guarantee amounting Tk. 
1,47,49,200/- for non-compliance with the order of the Ministry of Commerce, 
which has been furnished by Social Islami Bank Limited, Shyamoli Branch, 
Dhaka. 
It further appears from the submissions of the learned Advocate for the 
respondent-applicants that subsequent to the filing of the present writ petition, 
the petitioner has filed another writ petition being Writ Petition No. 10597 of 
2024, wherein the petitioner has challenged the letter of encashment dated 
19.08.2024 pertaining to the same Performance Guarantee amounting to Tk. 
1,47,49,200/- and arising out of Contract No. 24/21-22. 
On examination, it is evident that both the writ petitions are related to the 
same subject-matter, concerning the identical Bank Guarantee, and involving the 
same contractual dispute between the parties. The issues raised in Writ Petition 
No. 10597 of 2024 now substantially cover and encompass the matters 
originally agitated in the present writ petition. Moreover, the instant writ petition 
involves issues regarding commercial contract which cannot be adjudicated in 
the instant writ petition and therefore the instant writ petition is not 
maintainable. 
Accordingly, the application for discharging the Rule is allowed and the 
Rule issued in the instant writ petition is hereby discharged. 
 
 
 
 
 
        (Sikder Mahmudur Razi, J:)  
                                                  
(Raziuddin Ahmed, J:) 
","The PETITIONER sought writ relief against the STATE and other RESPONDENTS over a performance guarantee furnished for a commercial contract. The grievance concerned possible encashment of the guarantee and non-compliance with a ministry order regarding refund of the security. RESPONDENT Nos. 2 and 3 apply for termination of the Rule. They state that the PETITIONER later instituted a separate writ challenging the encashment letter dated 19.08.2024, arising from the identical guarantee and contract. According to those RESPONDENTS, the later proceeding concerns the same security and contractual controversy. They seek closure of the earlier proceeding on the basis of that overlap. No particular statutory provision is identified in the parties’ submissions recorded in the judgment.",Not stated,REFUSED,"The court compared the two writ proceedings and found that they concerned the same performance guarantee, the same contract and the same parties’ commercial dispute. It considered the challenges in the later petition to encompass substantially all matters raised in the earlier one. The court additionally held that the controversy concerned a commercial contract and was not suitable for adjudication in writ jurisdiction. Those findings about overlapping subject-matter and maintainability, rather than any named statutory provision, formed the basis for terminating the earlier Rule.",91ce5c5e06fa840014bbfdd1255219c7a247ef08fc2714701ad93387079ed80d
