","The PETITIONER, a defendant co-sharer, seeks revision under section 115(1) of the Code of Civil Procedure of the order dated 30.05.1999 concerning separate allotment in a partition suit. The PETITIONER sought .0823 satak, relying on a share in jointly purchased land and an additional four sataks purchased through a separate registered deed. The executing court allotted only the .0423 satak recognized by the earlier decree. The PETITIONER argues that the separate purchase is unchallenged and additional allotment would not diminish the OPPOSITE PARTIES’ shares. The OPPOSITE PARTIES contend that the separate purchase was not pleaded with the necessary claim or court fee, was not adjudicated, and cannot enlarge the executable decree. The dispute concerns the extent of allotment available in the pending partition proceedings.",Code of Civil Procedure 1908,PARTLY,"UNCERTAIN: The final order disposes of the revision with directions rather than expressly determining the requested allotment; PARTLY reflects the limited opportunity for reconsideration. The court found no legal error in restricting allotment to the share established by the preliminary decree because the separate purchase had not been adjudicated. Nevertheless, it considered that the PETITIONER might hold a valid additional title and should not be driven into another suit after prolonged litigation. It directed reconsideration of that purchase, including its validity, coverage by the schedule and any challenge to it, while preserving the OPPOSITE PARTIES’ allotted shares.",2999167859d99677cf1be0e01802dc8ffe28d3efc82122dc799938d363d33b80
