","The PETITIONER brought writ proceedings against the STATE and creditor RESPONDENTS concerning an auction of mortgaged property for recovery of loan dues. An order dated 27.01.2025 provided interim protection subject to an initial payment of Tk. 5,00,000 by 27.07.2025 and payment of the remaining arrears through twelve equal instalments by 27.07.2026. It also specified consequences for non-compliance. RESPONDENT No. 4, the creditor bank, seeks closure of the Rule and withdrawal of the interim protection. It relies on a bank certificate dated 14.11.2025, asserts that no agreed payments were made and states that no compliance affidavit was filed. The application further points to the limited duration of the interim arrangement and seeks continuation of the recovery process.",Not stated,REFUSED,"The court compared the creditor RESPONDENT’S allegations with its earlier conditional order. That order required an initial deposit followed by twelve instalments and prescribed an automatic consequence if the PETITIONER defaulted. Accepting the bank’s account that the required payments had not been made, the court found the conditions unsatisfied. It treated the stipulated consequence as already operating, so the Rule could no longer continue. The reasoning concerned enforcement of the payment conditions and did not determine the underlying loan dispute by reference to any identified statute.",9e20b3fbcd15494b9ed0f54c76026e94ae097b23c9348b1700a37121be3e2216
