","The PETITIONER, an industrial gas consumer, sought relief under Article 102 of the Constitution against the STATE and the gas-distribution RESPONDENT over failure to determine representations dated 29.06.2025, 07.07.2025 and 02.09.2025. The Rule sought a declaration concerning that inaction and a direction for determination. The PETITIONER later requested a supplementary Rule concerning a disconnection report dated 23.06.2025 and restoration of its gas supply. The distribution RESPONDENT offered reconnection upon payment of all assessed dues, including through instalments. The PETITIONER disputed both the amount claimed and the allegation of an unauthorized or bypass connection. The controversy additionally concerns which forum should examine the factual and billing issues underlying the disconnection and the proposed conditions for restoring supply.",Not stated,REFUSED,"The court found that the original grievance was administrative inaction, and the distribution RESPONDENT had since answered the representations and communicated its decision. The remaining controversy concerned the correctness of the bill and allegations of an unauthorized connection. Because the PETITIONER disputed those matters rather than accepting the proposed instalment arrangement, their resolution required factual investigation unsuitable for writ jurisdiction. The court identified the energy regulatory commission as the appropriate adjudicative forum. With the representations determined, it considered the original purpose of the proceedings fulfilled and found no surviving issue requiring adjudication.",cff4c948e0c3bff79ab9684e244770404ff61bda4920762922ce94ae083424df
