","The PETITIONER, an heir of a judgment-debtor, challenges the execution court’s order dated 14.05.2024 concerning an application to stay an auction of mortgaged property. The writ seeks a declaration that the order lacks lawful authority and protection for the property against the proposed sale. The application underlying that order asserted that the same property was included in another pending loan suit brought by a different creditor. The creditor RESPONDENT in the execution proceedings applies for termination of the Rule and withdrawal of interim protection. The materials record that the other creditor appeared before the execution court and expressed no objection to the auction. The dispute concerns the effect of the overlapping loan proceedings and that creditor’s position on the requested stay. No specific statutory provision is identified as the basis of the challenge.",Not stated,REFUSED,"The court examined the writ papers and the application that produced the challenged execution order. Although another creditor had included the property in a pending loan suit, that creditor appeared before the execution court and expressly had no objection to the auction. In those circumstances, the court found no illegality or infirmity in the execution court’s treatment of the stay application. Its reasoning rested on the other creditor’s stated position and the absence of a demonstrated defect in the order, rather than on interpretation of any identified statute.",4b5e975ea0260a0498dc6573b0962d80d3165d0f7578817c322a9976717e3e8c
