(Fatema Najib, J)","The PETITIONERS, members of a trade association, sought directions under Article 102 of the Constitution requiring reconstitution of the association’s Election Board and Election Appeal Board. They relied on an official memorandum dated 18.05.2025 ordering reconstitution and alleged that the existing boards continued election activities despite that direction. They also alleged obstruction in paying membership fees and sought a fresh electoral process. The STATE and association RESPONDENTS contested maintainability and voter status, relying on the Trade Organization Act, 2022, related rules, arbitration remedies and allegations of fabricated fee payments. The proceeding concerns compliance with the reconstitution direction and the lawfulness of continuing the election process under the existing boards.",Not stated,ALLOWED,"The court did not resolve the disputed questions of membership, voter status or maintainability. It relied on the STATE’s express statement that, because the earlier election date had passed, there was no objection to reconstituting the Election Board and Election Appellate Board to secure a fair election. On that basis, the court directed reconstitution in accordance with law within thirty days. The reasoning rested on the RESPONDENTS’ concession and the need for a lawful electoral process rather than on interpretation of a named statute.",652a8553a7e56ae83b30a63823bbeeed56ee485ac12946ae8db0e65982594752
