     (Fatema Najib, J) 
 
","The PETITIONER, the mother of a minor child, invoked Article 102 of the Constitution seeking production of the child and relief against alleged unlawful custody by the father and his family. She stated that after divorce she was prevented from meeting her daughter and did not know the child’s whereabouts. She alleged that the father’s drug addiction and rehabilitation treatment made his custody unsafe, and that an agreement waiving her custody claim was signed under pressure. The father’s side relied on that agreement and sought to retain custody. The proceeding concerns the child’s immediate safety, the mother’s access and custody, the father’s visitation, and the relationship between interim constitutional relief and a future Family Court custody determination.",Not stated,ALLOWED,"The court considered the child’s expressed willingness to stay with her mother, the affection observed between them, and the allegations concerning the father’s addiction and absence. It concluded that the child would be safe and better cared for in the mother’s custody at that stage. The asserted custody-waiver agreement was left for determination in a proper Family Court proceeding, which had not yet been initiated. The court balanced the mother’s immediate custody with the father’s scheduled visitation and virtual access, while preserving the Family Court’s authority to decide custody rights later.",1970183e08379735b75f5ad61321fc024c7ac5e260f7eba9442023341f56b0a0
