(Fatema Najib, J)","The PETITIONER, a government medical college lecturer, challenged the approval of an ad-hoc school committee so far as it nominated a person outside the headmaster’s proposed panel as president. He sought his own nomination as president, relying on regulations 39(1)(Ka) and 64(3) of the 2009 Regulations governing governing bodies and managing committees. The education-board RESPONDENTS relied on the 2024 Regulations, complaints against the headmaster and the proposed candidate, an inquiry report, and regulation 64(4), which permits nomination of another person in special circumstances. The proceeding concerns the applicable regulatory framework and the lawfulness of the board’s nomination.","Other: Secondary and Higher Secondary Education Board, Dinajpur (Governing Body and Managing Committee) Regulations, 2024",REFUSED,"The court found that the school was governed by the 2024 Regulations rather than the 2009 Regulations invoked by the PETITIONER. Regulation 64(4) permitted the board, in special circumstances, to nominate a person other than those proposed as president. Complaints against the headmaster and the proposed candidate, an inquiry report containing allegations against them, and a proposal from the deputy commissioner’s office supplied the circumstances for that course. The board’s nomination therefore had a regulatory basis, and the committee’s tenure had also expired, leaving no ground for interference.",afa85534371d66d6e2bcba03ce5c8924322c64c18e1e0c4efaea8cb310491d3f
