Farah Mahbub, J: 
 
 
In this Rule Nisi, issued under Article 102 of the Constitution of the 
People’s Republic of Bangladesh, the respondent no.1, Bangladesh Bank  
has been called upon to show cause as to why it should not be directed to 
provide information regarding Beximco Pharmaceutical Limited, respondent 
no.3 including all other business concerns of Beximco Group of Companies 
of Salman F. Rahman, respondent no.4 and also, as to how much unpaid 
loan said respondent No.4 had obtained from all banks and financial 
institutions including the present status of loans and repayment thereof.  
In the said Rule Nisi, the respondent no.1 was further directed to show 
cause as to why a receiver should not appointed to manage the companies of 
Beximco Group and attach all the properties belonging to the said Group of 
Companies.  
          Vide the interim order this Court directed the respondent no.1 to 
appoint a receiver in order to manage the companies of Beximco Group and 
to attach all the properties belonging to the said group of companies, 
however, for a prescribed period. At the same time, respondent no.1 has 
been further directed to recover the money obtained by the respondent no.4 
as loan from different banks and to bring the money back to Bangladesh 
from abroad.  
Respondent no.3, Beximco Pharmaceuticals Ltd., represented by its 
Managing Director, being aggrieved with the interim order of direction dated 
05.09.2024 moved before the Hon’ble Appellate Division by filing Civil 
Petition for Leave to Appeal No.3174 of 2024. The Appellate Division upon 
hearing the contending parties stayed the operation of the interim order 
passed by this Court so far as it related to the appointment of a receiver in 

<<PAGE 3>>
 
3 
respect of respondent no.3 only, till disposal of the Rule, with direction upon 
this Bench to hear and dispose of this Rule on merit, within a prescribed 
period and accordingly, had disposed of the said CPLA vide order dated 
12.11.2024. 
          Instant writ petition has been filed at the instance of the petitioner, a 
practicing lawyer of the Supreme Court of Bangladesh with 45(forty five) 
years of standing, who volunteered a number of public interest litigations 
involving the issue of unconstitutional assumption  of the office of the Care- 
taker Government by the then President of Bangladesh in addition to holding 
the office of the President including, among others, the issue of 
constitutional  obligation of the Election Commission to hold the general 
election of Bangladesh within 90 (ninety) days.  
         In the present writ petition, the categorical assertion of the petitioner, 
however, is that Beximco Pharmaceutical Ltd., respondent no.3 obtained a 
loan which stood at over Tk. 5000,00,00,000/-(Taka five thousand crore) 
from different banks. Instead of paying back the loan amount the respondent 
no.4 managed to procure a notification from the Ministry of Finance 
providing him extraordinary relief stating, inter alia, that anyone having 
loan liability over five thousand crore taka would not have to pay the loan 
for the next 25(twenty five) years and that it would pay whatever amount it 
choose to pay after the expiry of the said period. Further assertion of the 
petitioner is that Beximco Group had obtained a loan of twenty two 
thousand crore from a scheduled bank and no payment was made to 
reimburse the said loan amount.  
           Meanwhile, respondent no.1, in compliance with the interim direction 
given by this Court at the time of issuance of Rule on 05.09.2024, filed 

<<PAGE 4>>
 
4 
respective affidavits in compliance dated 27.11.2024, 04.12.2024, 
15.12.2024, 23.01.2025 and lastly, on 02.03.2025 annexing the respective 
official documents on the update position of the case and the steps so far it 
has taken in the matter in question.  
         In the affidavit in compliance particularly dated 02.03.2025 it has been 
stated, inter alia, that after having been communicated about the order of 
directions passed by this Court said respondent had issued letter on 
01.10.2024 to the Secretary, Ministry of Land for supplying the list of the 
