According to Circular No.26 of Bangladesh Financial Intelligence 
Unit (BFIU) dated 16.06.2020, all scheduled banks were under obligation to 
perform the Customer Due Diligence (CDD) while issuing loan facilities in 
order to identify the actual borrowers and actual beneficiaries of the loans, in 
order to minimize the risk of money laundering; the banks are also, required 
to take special measures while extending loans to the influential as well as 
politically exposed persons. Said circular has also, instructed the banks not 
to issue any loan where obligation to perfrom CDD becomes impossible.  
Moreover, under Section 27Ka of the Bank Companies Act, 1991, all 
banking and financial institutions are under obligation to send the defaulters’ 
list to the CIB of Bangladesh Bank. But some of the banks, which had 
granted further loan to the respective companies of Beximco Group, had 
hidden the classified status of the companies’ previous loans. They also, did 
not send clear picture of the loan status of those companies of Beximco 
Group to the CIB of Bangladesh Bank, which is a punishable offence under 
Section 31 read with Section 109 of the said Act, 1991. 
