Kashem/B.O","The PETITIONER, a Palli Bidyut Samity, challenged an ex parte Labour Court stay obtained in a complaint by a lineman who had been transferred and attached to the Rural Electrification Board’s Human Resource Directorate. The employee RESPONDENT relied on sections 213 and 216(1)(chha) of the Bangladesh Labour Act, 2006. The PETITIONER argued that sections 25 and 31 of the Rural Electrification Board Act, 2013 excluded the employee from the definition of “worker” in section 2(65) of the Labour Act, depriving the Labour Court of jurisdiction. At the hearing, the employee had already joined the new post, and the PETITIONER sought a formal direction to end the delay in the labour case. The dispute concerns the interim stay, jurisdiction and disposal of the pending complaint.",Not stated,REFUSED,"UNCERTAIN: the Rule was disposed of without adjudicating the merits, so the principal challenge to the stay order was not decided. The court observed that the employee was already serving in the transferred post and that the labour case had stalled because of the writ. It considered that justice would be best served by directing the Labour Court to dispose of the complaint expeditiously, preferably within six months, rather than examining the jurisdictional objection. No deciding statute was identified.",f9aaafd6a8abb514f4bce6e6bfd2aae362db466a8cf88857e41f926b39934fd4
1550-1578,Civil Revision No. 1354 of 2016,2025-07-03,"
